  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched with a kick-off on June 15th, led by Sarah Tan, with an initial phase budget of $500,000. The project has expanded its team with Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). It has secured strategic partnerships with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology. Key milestones include the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, with upcoming phases focusing on user interface enhancements (starting in October) and development (starting next month, led by Omar Jensen). Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase using AI algorithms, to be discussed in a meeting on August 5th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. Additionally, a separate entity, Zenith Innovations, was onboarded for a 'Revolutionary AI Project' with an onboarding session on April 15th, 2023."
